static.text.41=How this world connects
static.text.42=Symbol standardisation meets collection. USSO sets the principles; Symbolencyclopedia preserves the archive.
static.text.43=CED provides the energy that NODE LAB puts to use: a path from foundational technology to consciousness transfer.
static.text.44=BIB stands in opposition to NODE LAB’s digitisation, defending the body and physical existence.
static.text.45=The nation and the optimised language that supports it have separate resources. Explore the world setting alongside its grammar reference.
static.text.46=onva ⇄ Waon Jinkoku
static.text.47=A nation pursuing reason and optimisation contrasts with one shaped by harmony, order and staff culture. Together, they establish the philosophical balance of the world.
static.text.48=Layers of time
static.text.49=WAC → The whole world
static.text.50=An observatory recording changes in organisations, nations and ideas over time. It brings the world together through a shared chronology.
static.text.51=Artist R → Symbols & expression
static.text.52=Treating symbols as artworks as well as assets creates a bridge between institutions and art.
static.text.53=AI Fictional Dictionary → Possible worlds
static.text.54=By recording intelligences that do not exist, this archive expands the possibilities of the world itself.
static.text.55=Murinsu → Where questions begin
static.text.56=Thought begins here: a place for generating questions rather than delivering answers.
static.text.57=WORLD PORTAL COMPLETE EDITION · One connected view of gateways, archives, ideas, conflicts, futures, nations, languages and history.
